# A `uses: $/.github/actions/<name>` step makes the runner download this
# repository's archive at the workflow's commit and extract it, and extraction
# fails at "Set up job" on a symlink whose target the archive does not hold
# ("Could not find file .../.claude/skills"). These point into the git-ignored
# .savoir/ clone (and .agents/agents through .claude/agents), so they dangle in
# every archive. Leave them out of archives; checkouts keep them. A new
# dangling symlink fails scripts/ci/check-actions-lock.sh.
.claude/agents export-ignore
.claude/rules export-ignore
.claude/skills export-ignore
.agents/agents export-ignore
